{
  "dom_id": "step-e14551",
  "name": "Example: Dividing a Whole Number by a Non-Unit Fraction",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/60034ce6b9e7e7e5cd24c8f6f2f3d80a1bbc5d3a8532f3c4ccaeb3d89eaaeb1d.png)\n\n \n\nUse the model above to calculate the value of $2 \\div \\dfrac{3}{7}.$",
  "worked_solution": "To calculate ${\\color{red}2} \\div \\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{3}}{\\color{blue}7}$, we first need to divide each of the $\\color{red}2$ wholes into $\\color{blue}7$ equal parts.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/a373e9e5c6a5dc23240029d2d89fef66f4b9959ffef349f5ea351fffc897d3c8.png)\n\n \n\nNext, we break this into groups of $\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{3}$:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144806/assets/1cfe8f5a08ee9464489cacef94b0d94982def065a9ab290acc9ebbec6efc7bf7.png)\n\n \n\nNote the following: \n\n- We got $\\fbox{4}$ full groups.\n\n- There are $\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{2}$ pieces left over out of a possible group of $\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{3}.$ So the fractional part of our answer is \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{2}}{\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n2 \\div \\dfrac{3}{7} = \\fbox{4} \\, \\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, Moccasin]{2}}{\\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{3}}.\n$$",
